      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1885 Morton Grove opened its first greenhouses, heating 135,000 tons of coal each year to grow roses that won a 1904 St. Louis competition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morton_Grove%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Jazz Age, nightclubs like the Dells, Lincoln Tavern, and Coconut Grove turned Morton Grove into a speakeasy hotspot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morton_Grove%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village’s first Catholic parish began in 1919, renting a former tavern before building its own church in 1923.",
